A||||6||BAM-BAM||Door Glass?||||5||
Z||000000||BAM-BAM||04-23-2000||09:52 PM||||   Hey y'all. Just wondering if anyone has an easy way to replace scratched up door glass. I found a pair in an  88 Formula in the wrecking yard that are crystal clear. I need to know how to remove them and reinstall them in my 85GT. I know you guys have the tricks for this. The Haynes manual does not explain this part, only how to adjust the glass. TIA for any advise.<P> Thanx, BAM-BAM  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P> P.S. I have power windows <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||TOM||04-23-2000||11:44 PM||||You need to drill the track and stops from the glass then pull it up out of the door. To reinstasll use locknut and bolts||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gokart||04-24-2000||06:52 AM||||Get with someone like Tom or anyone who has successfully done this and find out what bit to use ect. I tried to do this in my parts car and as soon as I hit the power on my drill on the metal pin in the round white plastic stop, the whole door glass shattered! Ended up getting one from Kickhill Farm.||||reg||1
Z||000003||BAM-BAM||04-24-2000||07:02 AM||||  Tom, is there any particular way in which to do this without the glass shattering? Gokart mentioned that he had a problem with this. I would hate to get stuck without a window. Let me know please <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>  TIA, BAM-BAM  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||5
Z||000004||pollock||04-24-2000||09:34 AM||||I used to work at a glass shop, and had to drill out those rivets all the time.  <P>Our best trick was to take a rubber BMFH and wedge it between the bracket where the rivets are and the inside of the door.  This way you can hammer out the rivet shafts.  Then drill out the rivet bodies with a 1/4 inch drill.  Never broke a glass doing this.  Knock on wood.<P>Using the 1/4 inch bolts and lock nuts is a pretty good idea.  I found a deal on a Chinese knockoff of a Big Daddy Riveter for 16.99!  from Harbor Freight tools.  Low quality, but it'll do for the home user.<P>||||reg||6
Z||000005||theogre||04-24-2000||07:34 PM||||Not sure with Fiero, but most cars I can get the glass out with the track on. They where nearly all installed this way. It's really tricky in some doors. Worst one I ever did where rear windows in convertibles.<P>I'd rather take off the outer skin of the door than try drilling out the rivits. Unless the rivits are loose I like to leave them. It's not hard to take off the skin. cost about $3 for new bottom fasteners.||||reg||1
Z||000006||BAM-BAM||04-25-2000||01:01 AM||||     Thanks guys, I'll try on the wrecking yard windows first, that way I'll only be out a little money.<P> Thanx Again, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
